  "details": "Using the quick menu in desktop mode should not cause interactions with a world's UI elements.\n# Description\n1. Start VRChat in desktop mode\n2. Hover over a world UI element (i. e. a post processing toggle)\n3. Open your quick menu\n4. Navigate the quick menu by clicking on elements\n# Expected behaviour\nThe user can interact with the quick menu without affecting the world UI.\n# Actual behaviour\nEach click of the left mouse button affects both the quick menu and the world UI.\n# Notes\nA user may accidently hover over a world's UI, i. e. a post-processing toggle. Normally this shows a blue cursor, which is hidden when opening the quick menu. The user may affect that UI element without realizing.\n\nThis behaviour seems like a but to me. But if it's intended, then the blue cursor should probably be shown even if the quick menu is open.",
